1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,646
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,730 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,485 --> 00:00:29,738
[Ivy] <i>I'm going to gain</i>
<i>Divine Oytengco's trust.</i>

6
00:00:29,821 --> 00:00:32,282
-[Diego] <i>By bribing her?</i>
<i>-I was the one who bought that.</i>

7
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:33,491
<i>Ivy Aguas?</i>

8
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:37,454
<i>We'll work together</i>
<i>and we'll bring Emilia down.</i>

9
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:41,708
<i>We'll protect you and your kids.</i>

10
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:43,168
<i>Just trust me, Divine.</i>

11
00:00:43,585 --> 00:00:45,879
<i>A CCTV camera recorded</i>
<i>Divine Oytengco being kidnapped.</i>

12
00:00:45,962 --> 00:00:48,465
<i>Two men blew the tires</i>
<i>off the bodyguard's cars</i>

13
00:00:48,548 --> 00:00:49,674
<i>so they couldn't follow.</i>

14
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:53,636
[Natalie] <i>Then force Madrigal</i>
<i>to work for you again.</i>

15
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:55,930
<i>Just kill him after the mission.</i>

16
00:00:56,014 --> 00:00:57,390
<i>Keep an eye on Raul's group.</i>

17
00:00:57,474 --> 00:00:59,100
<i>Find out if they're planning something.</i>

18
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:01,561
<i>And just like what I did to Emilia,</i>

19
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:02,771
<i>I will also sabotage their plans.</i>

20
00:01:02,854 --> 00:01:04,397
[Diego] <i>Is this really Jaguar's hideout?</i>

21
00:01:04,481 --> 00:01:05,273
[Ivy] <i>Yes, it's here.</i>

22
00:01:05,356 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>I had them followed after</i>
<i>we met at the restaurant.</i>

23
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:10,320
<i>What did I ever do to you?</i>
<i>I'm your most loyal man!</i>

24
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:11,196
[Raul] <i>To me? Nothing.</i>

25
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:12,864
<i>But to my son? A lot.</i>

26
00:01:12,947 --> 00:01:14,157
<i>Say your prayers.</i>

27
00:01:17,952 --> 00:01:18,953
<i>Madrigal!</i>

28
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:21,331
[Ivy] <i>I'm just worried about Jepoy.</i>

29
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:24,876
<i>I hope he's all right. I hope he's alive.</i>

30
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,003
<i>-Ivy.</i>
<i>-Jepoy, where are you?</i>

31
00:01:27,086 --> 00:01:28,213
[Ivy] <i>I want you to come home.</i>

32
00:01:28,838 --> 00:01:31,090
<i>Ivy, I don't know where I am.</i>

33
00:01:31,466 --> 00:01:32,675
<i>Surprised?</i>

34
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:34,511
<i>You?</i>

35
00:01:34,594 --> 00:01:35,887
[Jepoy] <i>What do you really want?</i>

36
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,472
<i>Why did you save me from Jaguar?</i>

37
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:41,142
<i>I want you to work for me.</i>
<i>Let's take Jaguar down.</i>

38
00:01:45,188 --> 00:01:46,981
Once the case has been filed to the court,

39
00:01:47,065 --> 00:01:50,193
it will then be raffled to the judge
who will handle the case.

40
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:56,407
[Georgina] <i>Then the court shall</i>
<i>determine the probable cause</i>

41
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:58,785
<i>before they issue</i>
<i>an arrest warrant for Emilia.</i>

42
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:00,453
[ominous music playing]

43
00:02:00,537 --> 00:02:01,454
[door opening]

44
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,499
Attorney Fisher, please wait here.

45
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,334
Ombudsman Alfonso is on his way.

46
00:02:06,417 --> 00:02:07,460
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

47
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:10,171
We are finally here, Diego.

48
00:02:10,672 --> 00:02:11,965
-Yes, Attorney.
-[door opening]

49
00:02:12,674 --> 00:02:13,883
Ombudsman Alfonso.

50
00:02:14,551 --> 00:02:17,053
Mr. Diego Torillo. Attorney Fisher.

51
00:02:17,428 --> 00:02:18,471
Have a seat.

52
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,098
What can I do for you?

53
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,933
We are here to file a criminal case

54
00:02:22,016 --> 00:02:24,394
against former governor Emilia Ardiente.

55
00:02:24,477 --> 00:02:26,563
Here are some of the documents
that we found

56
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:29,107
that will serve as evidence to our case.

57
00:02:31,192 --> 00:02:32,819
[pensive music playing]

58
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:34,404
[Anna] <i>Diego is in court right now…</i>

59
00:02:34,487 --> 00:02:35,989
filing the case.

60
00:02:36,823 --> 00:02:40,702
There will be bloodshed
if the Ardientes try to stop us.

61
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,165
Mark my words.

62
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:53,214
How are you a victim of the Ardientes too?

63
00:02:53,590 --> 00:02:54,632
[raindrops pattering]

64
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,053
[pensive music continues]

65
00:02:59,137 --> 00:03:00,138
Well, Divine…

66
00:03:03,975 --> 00:03:07,896
Emilia is against
my relationship with Arnaldo.

67
00:03:08,313 --> 00:03:09,439
That's it.

68
00:03:09,814 --> 00:03:12,025
That's all I can say for now.

69
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:21,117
I'll help you until we win the case.

70
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:25,622
But please let me see my kids.

71
00:03:26,372 --> 00:03:27,999
I want to talk to them.

72
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:33,838
[sobbing] Please.

73
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:43,473
Mrs. Emilia, Mama has been gone
for two days now.

74
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,976
Her closest friends are saying
she's just on a vacation

75
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,978
but, Auntie, look what I found.

76
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:51,856
[tense music playing]

77
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,775
She's not even picking up her phone.

78
00:03:54,817 --> 00:03:55,610
Yeah.

79
00:03:56,277 --> 00:03:58,196
I saw the CCTV footage.

80
00:03:58,947 --> 00:04:00,782
Two men abducted your mom.

81
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,327
Mrs. Emilia, no one's
even contacting us for ransom.

82
00:04:04,953 --> 00:04:06,079
What's wrong with Mommy?

83
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,956
Is she involved in something bad?

84
00:04:08,039 --> 00:04:09,207
Please, Mrs. Emilia.

85
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:13,378
What's happening to Mommy? Why my mother?

86
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:16,464
Don't worry, okay?

87
00:04:17,173 --> 00:04:18,466
But can you do me a favor?

88
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:21,094
If ever you hear anything from your mom,

89
00:04:21,177 --> 00:04:22,762
can you please update me?

90
00:04:22,845 --> 00:04:25,348
And if ever she calls me, I'll update you.

91
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:27,809
-Okay?
-Okay, I will.

92
00:04:27,892 --> 00:04:29,644
Don't worry. I'll take care of everything.

93
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:35,692
[tense music continues]

94
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:44,534
[Ivy] <i>Emergency?</i>
<i>What happened? Are you okay?</i>

95
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:47,996
<i>Somebody is snooping in my old playground.</i>

96
00:04:48,246 --> 00:04:50,540
<i>Well, at least, you know it isn't me.</i>

97
00:04:51,082 --> 00:04:55,336
<i>Someone is investigating</i>
<i>your little committee.</i>

98
00:04:55,420 --> 00:05:00,216
[Julio] <i>They're trying to find</i>
<i>out how you stole funds</i>

99
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,426
<i>worth millions.</i>

100
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:02,593
<i>I wouldn't be surprised…</i>

101
00:05:02,677 --> 00:05:05,138
<i>if I find out that Ms. Aguas</i>

102
00:05:05,221 --> 00:05:08,099
<i>is behind the investigations against you!</i>

103
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:11,602
[Emilia] <i>Aunt Claire,</i>
<i>I haven't heard anything…</i>

104
00:05:11,686 --> 00:05:13,104
<i>from Divine, and I'm getting worried.</i>

105
00:05:13,187 --> 00:05:16,274
[Emilia] <i>Divine knows a lot</i>
<i>of my secrets, Aunt Claire.</i>

106
00:05:16,357 --> 00:05:17,150
<i>And guess what?</i>

107
00:05:17,233 --> 00:05:19,861
<i>I just saw Ivy Aguas at Divine's shop.</i>

108
00:05:19,944 --> 00:05:21,321
<i>I have a feeling that…</i>

109
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:24,282
<i>someone is going to use her against me,</i>

110
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,367
<i>and that's Ivy Aguas.</i>

111
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:28,036
[investigator] <i>A CCTV camera recorded</i>

112
00:05:28,119 --> 00:05:29,120
<i>Divine Oytengco being kidnapped.</i>

113
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:30,163
[Stephanie] <i>Mrs. Emilia,</i>

114
00:05:30,246 --> 00:05:32,248
<i>no one's even contacting us for ransom.</i>

115
00:05:32,665 --> 00:05:34,250
[Stephanie] <i>What's wrong with Mommy?</i>

116
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:36,085
<i>Is she involved in something bad?</i>

117
00:05:36,961 --> 00:05:38,463
[tense music playing]

118
00:05:39,589 --> 00:05:40,923
[line ringing]

119
00:05:41,340 --> 00:05:42,425
Hello, Samantha?

120
00:05:43,217 --> 00:05:45,553
Secure all my bank transactions

121
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:49,390
and call my former secretary
from city hall, now.

122
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:54,729
Hi, Emilia!

123
00:05:54,812 --> 00:05:56,189
[tense music playing]

124
00:05:56,272 --> 00:05:58,149
What are you doing here again?!

125
00:05:58,858 --> 00:06:03,571
I came here to visit Arnaldo.
And, well, to check on you too.

126
00:06:03,654 --> 00:06:06,032
What do you want? I have no time for this.

127
00:06:06,115 --> 00:06:09,077
I have no time for you!
I have important things to do.

128
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,537
Hold on, Emilia. Wait.

129
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:16,667
Um, can I stay here for a while?
I want to take care of Arnaldo.

130
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:18,377
Okay, do whatever you want, Ivy!

131
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,963
I have no time for this!
I have important things to do!

132
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:22,882
Someone's grumpy.

133
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:25,051
Are you on your period?
Where are you going?

134
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:29,138
It's none of your business. And wait!

135
00:06:30,932 --> 00:06:32,016
Just stay there.

136
00:06:32,975 --> 00:06:34,435
Don't you dare move!

137
00:06:36,020 --> 00:06:37,480
Don't start with me, Ivy.

138
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:41,359
[tense music playing]

139
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:46,322
Are you sure that's all of it?

140
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,533
Madam, these are the only files

141
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:50,368
left from when you were still mayor.

142
00:06:50,451 --> 00:06:52,578
Well, keep looking! Check them one by one!

143
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:56,958
You need to check
every single one of them!

144
00:06:57,041 --> 00:06:59,335
Do you understand?! Check them all!

145
00:06:59,418 --> 00:07:00,920
-Emilia!
-Shred this!

146
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:02,964
Emilia, what's going on?!

147
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:06,759
I'm trying to hide any evidence

148
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:08,886
they can use against me, Aunt Claire!

149
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,139
Someone has been keeping an eye on me!

150
00:07:11,222 --> 00:07:12,932
And who is that person?

151
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:15,435
Ivy Aguas.

152
00:07:16,227 --> 00:07:17,895
[tense music playing]

153
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:22,525
[heart rate monitor beeping]

154
00:07:28,364 --> 00:07:30,324
[beeping continues]

155
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:34,370
[slow tense music playing]

156
00:07:45,965 --> 00:07:47,091
[ominous music playing]

157
00:07:48,551 --> 00:07:49,719
Hi, Arnaldo.

158
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:54,640
Do you know why I'm still here?

159
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:00,313
To keep my friends close…

160
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:04,066
and my enemies closer.

161
00:08:09,739 --> 00:08:11,073
I'll be right here.

162
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:14,827
Because I want to keep an eye on you.

163
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:20,833
And to keep an eye on your mother too.

164
00:08:22,877 --> 00:08:24,921
So sleep well, Arnaldo.

165
00:08:25,838 --> 00:08:27,715
And don't ever wake up.

166
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:31,761
-[tense music playing]
-[beeping continues]

167
00:08:45,024 --> 00:08:46,651
[tense music playing]

168
00:08:47,276 --> 00:08:49,612
Ivy Aguas is back, Auntie!

169
00:08:49,987 --> 00:08:51,822
She's back at the mansion!

170
00:08:51,906 --> 00:08:53,449
And why would she want to be back

171
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,117
with all the hostility she's getting?!

172
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:57,286
Why would she want to be back, Auntie?!

173
00:08:57,620 --> 00:08:59,664
Because she's keeping an eye on me!

174
00:08:59,747 --> 00:09:00,706
She even went to…

175
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:02,083
-Emilia.
-…Divine's shop?

176
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:06,837
Emilia! Think straight
and go back to your senses!

177
00:09:07,171 --> 00:09:10,341
Do you want to go crazy like Arnaldo?!

178
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:14,345
Keep searching! Hurry! Check them all!

179
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:15,763
Mrs. Emilia, they're gone.

180
00:09:15,846 --> 00:09:17,974
Maybe Carol gave it to the woman
who came here before.

181
00:09:18,391 --> 00:09:19,767
Someone came here?

182
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:22,436
Yes, but it was Carol who spoke to her.

183
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:24,397
What did she look like?

184
00:09:25,731 --> 00:09:26,649
Well?!

185
00:09:30,319 --> 00:09:31,988
[ominous music playing]

186
00:09:32,446 --> 00:09:33,948
Oh, hi, Camia!

187
00:09:34,282 --> 00:09:35,616
[tense music playing]

188
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:37,994
Emilia, what are you doing here?

189
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:39,495
I'm paying you a visit!

190
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:41,205
Is that so wrong?

191
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:43,124
No wonder I wasn't feeling well.

192
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:46,669
It's as if the devil was heading my way.

193
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:49,422
And what do you think of yourself?

194
00:09:49,839 --> 00:09:52,592
You think you're a saint,
but all you are is a nosy woman.

195
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:55,511
You went through my files? Why?

196
00:09:55,595 --> 00:09:56,721
To have me investigated?

197
00:09:56,804 --> 00:09:57,555
Answer me!

198
00:09:58,389 --> 00:10:00,224
[tense music continues]

199
00:10:01,684 --> 00:10:02,977
You won't answer?

200
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:05,187
Well…

201
00:10:05,438 --> 00:10:07,690
I think this will change your mind!

202
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:11,485
[suspenseful music playing]

203
00:10:13,904 --> 00:10:16,699
Go ahead, Emilia! Kill me!

204
00:10:17,533 --> 00:10:18,993
That wouldn't be the worst thing

205
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:21,329
your sadistic family has done to me!

206
00:10:22,997 --> 00:10:24,665
You know, you are so right.

207
00:10:25,416 --> 00:10:26,500
You're right.

208
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:29,962
Papa and his hitman
should have just killed you!

209
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:31,547
I don't know why you're still alive!

210
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:34,675
I won't let someone
like you put me behind bars!

211
00:10:34,759 --> 00:10:35,760
Do you understand?!

212
00:10:35,843 --> 00:10:37,762
Yes, but you're going to die first!

213
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:39,221
[screaming] [coughing]

214
00:10:39,305 --> 00:10:40,348
[squealing]

215
00:10:40,431 --> 00:10:41,515
What?!

216
00:10:41,724 --> 00:10:43,351
[Loring] You bought so much.

217
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:44,560
You can't even eat half of that

218
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:46,312
-because of your diabetes.
-Kill joy! Kill joy!

219
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:47,146
Oh!

220
00:10:47,229 --> 00:10:48,606
Who was that guy? He looked suspicious?

221
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:49,482
-Wait…
-Hey.

222
00:10:49,565 --> 00:10:51,817
Did we leave the door open?

223
00:10:51,901 --> 00:10:52,860
-Guard!
-Guard!

224
00:10:52,943 --> 00:10:53,861
-Guard!
-Guard!

225
00:10:53,944 --> 00:10:55,154
-Hurry!
-Guard!

226
00:10:55,237 --> 00:10:55,988
Hey!

227
00:10:56,072 --> 00:10:57,156
Why are you here?!

228
00:10:57,698 --> 00:10:58,741
Come here!

229
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:00,743
-[clamoring]
-Wait!

230
00:11:02,745 --> 00:11:05,539
You bunch of poor people!

231
00:11:05,915 --> 00:11:06,999
Touching me?!

232
00:11:07,416 --> 00:11:08,459
[screaming]

233
00:11:08,542 --> 00:11:09,377
You!

234
00:11:09,460 --> 00:11:10,711
Don't you know who I am?

235
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:14,632
I am Emilia Ardiente.
I can buy you and this hospital!

236
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:17,593
Pathetic. Oh, but wait.

237
00:11:18,010 --> 00:11:21,472
Let me get my expensive bag
that you guys can't afford!

238
00:11:21,972 --> 00:11:23,516
[grunts]

239
00:11:27,395 --> 00:11:28,813
Don't ever come back!

240
00:11:28,896 --> 00:11:31,023
She's just like her evil father!

241
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:33,109
She's Lucifer's right hand!

242
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:34,985
-Camia, how are you?
-Goodness!

243
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,612
I'm all right now.

244
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:38,906
[breathing heavily]

245
00:11:41,033 --> 00:11:42,034
Miss Loring?

246
00:11:43,035 --> 00:11:44,662
[somber music playing]

247
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,080
What?!

248
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:48,749
What happened to my mother?

249
00:11:48,833 --> 00:11:50,042
She's fine now.

250
00:11:50,543 --> 00:11:54,713
[Loring] I don't know.
If we had come in a minute late,

251
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:57,550
I don't know
what would have happened to her.

252
00:11:58,509 --> 00:12:00,553
Emilia's insane.

253
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:04,765
Miss Loring, please let me
speak to my mother.

254
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:07,768
Your mom's resting now, dear.

255
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,770
Okay. Thank you, anyway.

256
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:10,980
All right, bye.

257
00:12:12,606 --> 00:12:14,942
[somber music playing]

258
00:12:21,031 --> 00:12:22,700
[sighing] Poof.

259
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:26,579
What are you still doing here?

260
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,875
My mission isn't finished yet.

261
00:12:31,834 --> 00:12:33,836
-"Mission."
-That's why I'm still here.

262
00:12:33,919 --> 00:12:35,588
Don't worry, Emilia.

263
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:38,424
I'll just finish my mission.

264
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:40,926
Okay.

265
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:43,304
You're speaking in tongues.

266
00:12:43,387 --> 00:12:44,180
"Mission."

267
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:47,600
[tense music playing]

268
00:13:04,658 --> 00:13:07,328
That Camia! I will kill her!

269
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:09,163
[Emilia] <i>I will strangle her neck, Auntie!</i>

270
00:13:09,246 --> 00:13:10,915
[Claire] <i>Calm down, Emilia.</i>

271
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,169
-I can't calm down!
-[mobile phone ringing]

272
00:13:15,669 --> 00:13:17,171
Hello? Yes, Attorney?

273
00:13:17,588 --> 00:13:20,466
[tense music playing]

274
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:21,967
What?!

275
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:25,095
Camia Cruz didn't file
the case against me?

276
00:13:26,263 --> 00:13:28,682
[Emilia] <i>No, but you still have</i>
<i>to get that woman!</i>

277
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:31,060
What?

278
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,478
I…

279
00:13:32,561 --> 00:13:34,063
I have a case with the Ombudsman?

280
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:38,317
Who filed it if Camia Cruz didn't?

281
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,154
Diego?

282
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:43,781
Oh my--

283
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:46,659
[screaming]

284
00:13:48,202 --> 00:13:50,037
[Emilia] <i>That Diego, Auntie!</i>

285
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:52,122
What am I going to do?

286
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,083
[tense music playing]

287
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:57,378
I need alcohol, Auntie. I need wine.

288
00:14:03,968 --> 00:14:04,969
[tense music swells]

289
00:14:05,261 --> 00:14:10,307
So, Ivy, I do apologize
for the late welcome.

290
00:14:10,641 --> 00:14:13,727
But I appreciate the effort
that you're putting in

291
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:15,354
to take care of Arnaldo.

292
00:14:17,398 --> 00:14:19,066
[Julio] How long will you be staying?

293
00:14:20,359 --> 00:14:21,777
Around a week.

294
00:14:22,319 --> 00:14:23,654
-One week?
-Mm-hm.

295
00:14:25,114 --> 00:14:26,991
Yeah, I guess one week is enough time

296
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:31,245
to be able to iron out the kinks
in our relationships.

297
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,122
Right, Emilia?

298
00:14:34,957 --> 00:14:38,419
Papa, having a rapport with Ivy right now

299
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,588
should be the least of my problems.

300
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:42,840
Just to remind you again,

301
00:14:42,923 --> 00:14:47,052
Papa, I have an ongoing plunder
case filed by Diego Torillo.

302
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:50,472
And he has Divine Oytengco.

303
00:14:51,098 --> 00:14:54,059
That's why they're not afraid
to file a case against me.

304
00:14:55,311 --> 00:14:56,937
You know that's not news to me.

305
00:14:57,396 --> 00:14:58,981
That case won't go anywhere.

306
00:15:00,232 --> 00:15:02,318
Even if Judge Nazareno
is handling the case?

307
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,737
Our family's enemy?

308
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,697
Wow, Papa.

309
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:09,283
I can just imagine if this goes south.

310
00:15:10,492 --> 00:15:14,747
How will this affect your candidacy?

311
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:17,207
[slow tense music playing]

312
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,961
Emilia.

313
00:15:21,045 --> 00:15:22,254
No, thank you.

314
00:15:24,214 --> 00:15:25,007
Sure?

315
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:26,175
Yes.

316
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,179
Thank you, my dear.

317
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:33,349
[Julio] Problems, problems…

318
00:15:34,141 --> 00:15:35,517
Minor problems…

319
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:38,562
Well, I hope, Papa, it's just minor.

320
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:40,940
A minor glitch.

321
00:15:42,066 --> 00:15:44,777
[tense music continues]

322
00:15:50,699 --> 00:15:51,450
[car honking]

323
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:53,202
Julio Ardiente,

324
00:15:54,161 --> 00:15:57,581
from the famed and fertile
lands of Poblacion Ardiente.

325
00:15:59,041 --> 00:16:00,709
I heard from my fellows

326
00:16:01,293 --> 00:16:04,964
that it was difficult for us
to deal with you Ardientes.

327
00:16:05,631 --> 00:16:07,341
For you, there are only two things.

328
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,760
Money or bullet.

329
00:16:11,470 --> 00:16:15,724
I see that my reputation precedes me.

330
00:16:16,725 --> 00:16:17,559
But…

331
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:23,357
I'm not going to say
that isn't true, Judge.

332
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:25,901
I just have one piece of advice.

333
00:16:26,610 --> 00:16:28,487
Reserve your killings for endeavors

334
00:16:28,570 --> 00:16:30,698
that will advance your agenda.

335
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,325
Let me paint you a scenario.

336
00:16:33,909 --> 00:16:35,411
Emilia will be tried

337
00:16:35,494 --> 00:16:37,997
because there is strong
evidence against her.

338
00:16:39,164 --> 00:16:40,749
She will be convicted…

339
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:43,585
but put in a comfortable jail.

340
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:45,754
You will lose a daughter.

341
00:16:47,172 --> 00:16:49,550
But you already know
that she gives you nothing.

342
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:53,387
In essence, you lose nothing.

343
00:16:55,472 --> 00:16:57,683
Why would you kill for nothing?

344
00:16:58,267 --> 00:17:01,395
[tense music playing]

345
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:05,899
[Joselito] <i>You were right.</i>

346
00:17:05,983 --> 00:17:08,569
Julio Ardiente came to me.

347
00:17:09,403 --> 00:17:10,320
<i>I told him…</i>

348
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,489
the exact words you told me to say.

349
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:16,118
Thank you. Thank you, Judge Nazareno.

350
00:17:16,577 --> 00:17:17,870
<i>I regret…</i>

351
00:17:17,953 --> 00:17:20,664
not meeting you sooner.

352
00:17:21,040 --> 00:17:23,709
I believe in what you're fighting for…

353
00:17:23,792 --> 00:17:26,754
<i>and your desire to expose…</i>

354
00:17:27,046 --> 00:17:28,672
…those corrupting the country.

355
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,509
I should be the one thanking you.

356
00:17:33,927 --> 00:17:35,971
Again, thank you, Judge Nazareno.

357
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:37,181
Bye.

358
00:17:38,057 --> 00:17:39,975
[suspenseful music playing]

359
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:44,563
Julio, you bastard. I knew it.

360
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,364
[ominous music playing]

361
00:17:54,698 --> 00:17:57,743
[Joselito] <i>Emilia will be tried</i>
<i>because there is strong evidence</i>

362
00:17:57,826 --> 00:17:59,036
<i>against her.</i>

363
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:00,621
<i>She will be convicted.</i>

364
00:18:01,288 --> 00:18:02,664
<i>You will lose a daughter.</i>

365
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,833
<i>But she gives you nothing.</i>

366
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,877
<i>In essence, you lose nothing.</i>

367
00:18:08,504 --> 00:18:10,506
[Joselito] <i>Why would you kill for nothing?</i>

368
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:13,926
Papa…

369
00:18:16,136 --> 00:18:18,514
Papa, did you talk to the judge already?

370
00:18:19,389 --> 00:18:21,225
Will they dismiss my case?

371
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:24,103
Am I going to jail?

372
00:18:25,562 --> 00:18:27,439
[tense music playing]

373
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:39,034
[sobbing]

374
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:42,538
[dramatic piano music playing]

375
00:18:43,789 --> 00:18:45,499
[sobbing]

376
00:18:50,754 --> 00:18:51,964
Mrs. Oytengco…

377
00:18:52,214 --> 00:18:53,006
Diego…

378
00:18:53,090 --> 00:18:54,508
I've already spoken with your children.

379
00:18:54,591 --> 00:18:55,384
Huh?

380
00:18:55,801 --> 00:18:57,094
You'll be reunited with them later.

381
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:58,011
Really?

382
00:19:02,182 --> 00:19:04,434
Thank you so much. Thank you.

383
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:07,688
[sobbing]

384
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,524
[Emilia] <i>Papa, answer me!</i>

385
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:12,276
Sit your ass down!

386
00:19:13,277 --> 00:19:14,319
And you, Ivy.

387
00:19:14,778 --> 00:19:16,196
Please, join us.

388
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:17,948
What is this about, Papa?!

389
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:23,036
What are you willing to do to
make sure you don't get jailed?

390
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:23,954
Oh my, Papa!

391
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:25,664
Why are you asking these silly questions?

392
00:19:25,747 --> 00:19:26,874
Not now, please!

393
00:19:26,957 --> 00:19:29,710
Will you just answer
the wretched question?!

394
00:19:30,961 --> 00:19:33,088
I don't know! Maybe, kill the judge?

395
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,716
Pay the judge? Or, kill the witnesses!

396
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,426
[tense music playing]

397
00:19:37,509 --> 00:19:38,635
How about you, Ivy?

398
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:42,264
If you were in her shoes,
what would you do?

399
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,227
Get the best lawyer, Congressman.

400
00:19:47,603 --> 00:19:48,395
Oh.

401
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:51,440
You, and you.

402
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:55,319
You are both very, very wrong.

403
00:19:55,402 --> 00:19:56,445
[tense music playing]

404
00:19:56,528 --> 00:19:58,030
Good grief, Emilia.

405
00:19:58,363 --> 00:20:02,951
If it were me, I'd destroy
the person who sued you!

406
00:20:03,452 --> 00:20:04,536
Goodness.

407
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,038
Such a simple solution.

408
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:11,460
You know, the root cause of our
problems is one and the same.

409
00:20:12,169 --> 00:20:14,254
From the very start,

410
00:20:14,338 --> 00:20:16,256
there's only been one thorn
on this family's side.

411
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:17,591
Diego Torillo!

412
00:20:19,635 --> 00:20:22,638
[suspenseful music playing]

413
00:20:24,598 --> 00:20:25,557
And I will put an end

414
00:20:25,641 --> 00:20:28,602
to the life of that miserable,
wretched worm.

415
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:34,566
[mobile phone ringing]

416
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:37,903
Hello? Stephanie, yes?

417
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:41,240
What?!

418
00:20:41,573 --> 00:20:42,449
Oh, really?

419
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,535
It's good to know you've finally
spoken with your mom.

420
00:20:46,411 --> 00:20:47,829
What? Wait.

421
00:20:47,913 --> 00:20:50,791
Did you just say that
she's with Diego Torillo?!

422
00:20:52,125 --> 00:20:54,336
No, I'm just going to stay here. Yeah.

423
00:20:55,087 --> 00:20:56,588
Good to hear from you again, sweetie.

424
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:59,341
I'm happy for you. Bye!

425
00:21:00,259 --> 00:21:02,678
[slow tense music playing]

426
00:21:03,553 --> 00:21:04,721
[line ringing]

427
00:21:04,805 --> 00:21:05,681
Hello!

428
00:21:06,014 --> 00:21:09,434
I heard Divine Oytengco
was seen with Diego Torillo.

429
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,186
Wait for them outside the restaurant,

430
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,980
then blow their car up to bits!

431
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:16,316
Make sure no one gets out alive!
Understand?!

432
00:21:21,113 --> 00:21:23,115
She's high-strung.

433
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:27,411
So violent.

434
00:21:29,538 --> 00:21:30,831
Excuse me, Congressman.

435
00:21:41,883 --> 00:21:44,469
[phone ringing]

436
00:21:45,387 --> 00:21:46,221
Hello, Ivy.

437
00:21:47,097 --> 00:21:47,889
Diego.

438
00:21:48,265 --> 00:21:52,602
Diego, don't go meet
Divine's children anymore.

439
00:21:52,978 --> 00:21:55,772
<i>Emilia's men are on</i>
<i>their way there. If we lose…</i>

440
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,399
our whistle-blower,

441
00:21:57,691 --> 00:22:00,110
all our plans will be for nothing.

442
00:22:01,069 --> 00:22:02,237
<i>Ivy, don't worry.</i>

443
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,948
I'm with Arthur, we'll take care of it.

444
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:08,994
Diego, promise me you won't get hurt.

445
00:22:09,077 --> 00:22:10,996
That none of you will get hurt.

446
00:22:11,538 --> 00:22:15,042
Ivy, I'll make sure the ones
on our side stay safe.

447
00:22:15,709 --> 00:22:16,585
Thank you.

448
00:22:17,961 --> 00:22:20,130
[tense music playing]

449
00:22:22,132 --> 00:22:23,050
What's wrong?

450
00:22:24,968 --> 00:22:27,220
Emilia's men are waiting
at the restaurant.

451
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:29,181
We have to go there
and get my children out!

452
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:31,183
Who knows what Emilia will do to them?!

453
00:22:32,476 --> 00:22:35,103
Don't worry. I have a plan.

454
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,397
Okay.

455
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:39,733
[suspenseful music playing]

456
00:22:57,918 --> 00:23:00,587
Are you enjoying
what you're watching right now?

457
00:23:06,384 --> 00:23:07,928
You know, Papa was right.

458
00:23:08,428 --> 00:23:11,264
He said, "You should
destroy your enemies."

459
00:23:12,224 --> 00:23:14,226
[ominous music playing]

460
00:23:14,851 --> 00:23:16,978
I should've done this a long time ago.

461
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:33,829
[tense music playing]

462
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:39,584
You must really like Diego.

463
00:23:41,837 --> 00:23:46,591
Actually, you must love him
more than you love Arnaldo.

464
00:23:48,051 --> 00:23:50,137
I can see it in your eyes, Ivy.

465
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:52,180
It's quite obvious.

466
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:57,394
But don't worry, it's over now.

467
00:24:03,108 --> 00:24:08,947
What does it feel like to talk
when no one's listening?

468
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:14,995
Even if they kill Diego Torillo
in front of me, I wouldn't care.

469
00:24:18,373 --> 00:24:19,416
I really don't.

470
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:32,095
[ominous music playing]

471
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:44,649
[gunshot]

472
00:24:47,319 --> 00:24:50,530
[gunshots]

473
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:58,038
[gunshots]

474
00:25:04,377 --> 00:25:06,671
<i>Emilia's men are waiting</i>
<i>at the restaurant.</i>

475
00:25:06,755 --> 00:25:08,548
<i>We have to go there</i>
<i>and get my children out!</i>

476
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:10,258
<i>Who knows what Emilia will do to them?!</i>

477
00:25:10,967 --> 00:25:13,637
<i>Don't worry. I have a plan.</i>

478
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:16,139
<i>Keep eating while we're waiting for Mommy.</i>

479
00:25:16,681 --> 00:25:17,849
[mobile phone ringing]

480
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:18,767
<i>It's Mama.</i>

481
00:25:20,060 --> 00:25:20,977
<i>Hello, Mama?</i>

482
00:25:21,061 --> 00:25:22,896
<i>Stephanie, you listen</i>
<i>to me carefully, okay?</i>

483
00:25:22,979 --> 00:25:24,481
<i>You have to leave right now.</i>

484
00:25:24,564 --> 00:25:27,776
[Divine] <i>Take the exit out the</i>
<i>back. I'll meet you there, okay?</i>

485
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:29,778
<i>Come on. Hurry.</i>

486
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:31,613
<i>Are you okay?</i>

487
00:25:31,696 --> 00:25:33,531
[tense music playing]

488
00:25:42,082 --> 00:25:43,083
<i>It's Mommy.</i>

489
00:25:48,672 --> 00:25:49,756
<i>Thank you. Thank you.</i>

490
00:25:51,967 --> 00:25:53,969
[Divine] <i>Let's go, let's go! Let's go!</i>

491
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:55,929
<i>Let's go. All set.</i>

492
00:25:56,012 --> 00:25:58,223
<i>-Come on. Come on. Careful.</i>
<i>-Get inside. Hurry, get in.</i>

493
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:01,393
<i>Get inside. Hurry, get in. Hurry! Go!</i>

494
00:26:03,561 --> 00:26:05,146
<i>How are you, kids?</i>

495
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:07,482
<i>Arthur, take care of them.</i>

496
00:26:07,565 --> 00:26:08,483
<i>-I'll handle it.</i>
<i>-Be careful.</i>

497
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:16,866
[suspenseful music playing]

498
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:30,338
[engine running]

499
00:26:34,050 --> 00:26:36,720
[gunshots]

500
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:40,807
[gunshots]

501
00:26:53,236 --> 00:26:55,280
[tense music playing]

502
00:27:07,667 --> 00:27:08,835
Where are they?

503
00:27:09,627 --> 00:27:10,628
There's nobody there?

504
00:27:18,261 --> 00:27:19,637
Oh, Emilia.

505
00:27:19,888 --> 00:27:20,764
[grunts]

506
00:27:32,442 --> 00:27:33,234
<i>Papa!</i>

507
00:27:33,526 --> 00:27:35,362
Diego got away, Divine got away.

508
00:27:35,445 --> 00:27:36,863
So, my case will continue?!

509
00:27:37,781 --> 00:27:41,076
But you spoke to Judge Nazareno.
Right, Papa?

510
00:27:41,159 --> 00:27:43,161
My case will be dismissed, right?!

511
00:27:43,661 --> 00:27:44,996
[somber music playing]

512
00:27:45,080 --> 00:27:45,830
Wrong.

513
00:27:46,623 --> 00:27:47,415
What?

514
00:27:49,125 --> 00:27:55,215
I'm not going to waste my money
or my bullets on nothing.

515
00:27:56,299 --> 00:27:58,468
You've got to be kidding me, Papa, right?

516
00:27:58,551 --> 00:28:00,178
You've got to be kidding me!

517
00:28:01,054 --> 00:28:02,680
I'm sorry, Emilia.

518
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:04,682
I'm not kidding.

519
00:28:07,352 --> 00:28:08,937
[dramatic music playing]

520
00:28:11,981 --> 00:28:13,191
[sighs]

521
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:31,918
Emilia!

522
00:28:36,464 --> 00:28:38,591
Emilia, you don't have to do this.

523
00:28:38,675 --> 00:28:40,885
I need to, Auntie. I'm going to jail.

524
00:28:40,969 --> 00:28:43,054
I need to leave right now.
I need to get on a plane!

525
00:28:45,890 --> 00:28:46,766
And you!

526
00:28:47,183 --> 00:28:49,102
Don't just stand there snickering.

527
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:51,604
I know you had something
to do with me going to jail.

528
00:28:52,021 --> 00:28:53,773
Me? Me again?

529
00:28:54,232 --> 00:28:56,818
Emilia, you're funny. You keep blaming me.

530
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:59,779
We were together the whole time.
How could I be involved in this?

531
00:29:00,238 --> 00:29:02,157
But fine. Go. Go, Emilia. Run.

532
00:29:02,449 --> 00:29:03,241
Ivy!

533
00:29:03,491 --> 00:29:05,326
I have no time for this, Ivy.

534
00:29:05,410 --> 00:29:07,370
Not now! Because I'm going to prison.

535
00:29:07,454 --> 00:29:10,957
Papa betrayed me.
Divine and that Diego are alive!

536
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:14,419
I'm going to prison, Auntie,
that's why I have to go.

537
00:29:14,502 --> 00:29:15,420
I'm leaving!

538
00:29:15,503 --> 00:29:17,213
-Emilia.
-Emilia, don't worry.

539
00:29:17,297 --> 00:29:19,466
If ever, I can visit you. Me and Mamita.

540
00:29:19,549 --> 00:29:20,508
[screaming]

541
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:22,343
[door opening]

542
00:29:23,261 --> 00:29:24,429
[tense music playing]

543
00:29:24,763 --> 00:29:25,597
[door closing]

544
00:29:26,681 --> 00:29:28,016
Go ahead, Emilia.

545
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:31,311
Run as far as your legs can carry you.

546
00:29:36,733 --> 00:29:37,817
Emilia, please.

547
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:40,361
Please don't do this.

548
00:29:42,113 --> 00:29:44,991
Emilia. Don't do this, Emilia.

549
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,242
Oh my goodness.

550
00:29:47,202 --> 00:29:48,995
[tense music continues]

551
00:29:57,587 --> 00:29:58,630
[mobile phone ringing]

552
00:30:00,256 --> 00:30:01,257
Ivy?

553
00:30:01,341 --> 00:30:03,384
Hello? Where are you?

554
00:30:03,468 --> 00:30:04,636
We're here.

555
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:06,971
Hurry up, Emilia's escaping.

556
00:30:07,222 --> 00:30:08,014
What?

557
00:30:16,272 --> 00:30:19,234
[suspenseful music playing]

558
00:30:24,531 --> 00:30:26,282
You won't get away, Emilia.

559
00:30:28,952 --> 00:30:30,036
[Julio] Open that gate.

560
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:36,000
What do you want?

561
00:30:36,084 --> 00:30:38,962
Give us Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.

562
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:40,421
[scoffs]

563
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:44,717
Who gave you the right to
tell me to give you my daughter?

564
00:30:45,718 --> 00:30:48,555
Where is Emilia
Ardiente-Torillo, Congressman?

565
00:30:48,638 --> 00:30:49,556
She isn't here.

566
00:30:50,515 --> 00:30:52,559
We have a warrant for her arrest.

567
00:30:54,394 --> 00:30:56,938
I don't care about your warrant of arrest.

568
00:30:57,605 --> 00:30:58,398
Julio!

569
00:30:59,190 --> 00:31:00,859
-Julio, what's happening?!
-I'm sorry, Congressman.

570
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,277
But, we received information

571
00:31:02,360 --> 00:31:03,987
that your daughter is here with you.

572
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:08,950
[tense music playing]

573
00:31:11,494 --> 00:31:13,121
Come on. Let's search the place.

574
00:31:13,204 --> 00:31:14,455
Didn't you hear me?!

575
00:31:15,206 --> 00:31:16,958
Get out of my property!

576
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:19,627
-Julio!
-You bastards!

577
00:31:19,919 --> 00:31:20,962
[Claire] Wait!

578
00:31:29,929 --> 00:31:30,972
-Diego.
-Ivy.

579
00:31:31,472 --> 00:31:33,725
-Emilia went that way.
-Follow me!

580
00:31:38,229 --> 00:31:39,480
Good luck, Emilia.

581
00:31:51,284 --> 00:31:52,076
Hello?

582
00:31:52,702 --> 00:31:53,912
Stephanie?

583
00:31:53,995 --> 00:31:54,913
Where are you?!

584
00:31:55,204 --> 00:31:56,539
I need the ticket!

585
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:58,917
[police siren wailing]

586
00:32:05,381 --> 00:32:06,257
Mrs. Emilia!

587
00:32:06,341 --> 00:32:08,927
Don't try to escape! Just come with us!

588
00:32:09,636 --> 00:32:11,471
[panting] No.

589
00:32:16,309 --> 00:32:17,477
Come on! Hurry!

590
00:32:24,817 --> 00:32:25,610
Emilia.

591
00:32:28,071 --> 00:32:29,030
Give up.

592
00:32:33,201 --> 00:32:35,453
[dramatic music playing]

593
00:32:43,544 --> 00:32:44,671
Emilia Torillo.

594
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:47,215
You are under arrest for plunder.

595
00:32:47,298 --> 00:32:50,426
You have the right to remain silent.

596
00:32:50,510 --> 00:32:54,097
Anything you say can
and will be used against you.

597
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:56,808
You have the right to an attorney.

598
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:58,685
If you can't afford an attorney,

599
00:32:58,768 --> 00:33:00,937
one will be provided by the government.

600
00:33:01,562 --> 00:33:03,356
You can't do this to me!

601
00:33:03,982 --> 00:33:05,608
Don't you know who I am?!

602
00:33:06,150 --> 00:33:08,027
I'm Emilia Ardiente!

603
00:33:08,403 --> 00:33:10,321
You cannot do this to me!

604
00:33:10,655 --> 00:33:11,572
Papa!

605
00:33:12,031 --> 00:33:13,616
Why are you just standing there?!

606
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:15,118
-You have to do something.
-Cuff her!

607
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:17,078
-No!
-There's nothing I can do.

608
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:20,873
No! Please! Papa! Do something!

609
00:33:21,207 --> 00:33:22,583
I'm sorry, Emilia.

610
00:33:23,626 --> 00:33:26,671
-[Julio] Please don't hurt her.
-Auntie!

611
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:32,176
[tense music playing]

612
00:33:42,478 --> 00:33:46,357
Auntie! Papa, please!

613
00:33:47,608 --> 00:33:49,861
[tense music continues]

614
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:06,127
[Ivy] <i>You basked in your wealth.</i>

615
00:34:06,836 --> 00:34:08,671
<i>Wealth that you used</i>

616
00:34:10,048 --> 00:34:11,924
<i>to kill my father…</i>

617
00:34:13,718 --> 00:34:14,635
[car crashing]

618
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:16,721
<i>…to hire someone to rape my mother…</i>

619
00:34:16,804 --> 00:34:18,056
[suppressed gunshots]

620
00:34:20,725 --> 00:34:22,685
<i>…and to intimidate others.</i>

621
00:34:30,359 --> 00:34:32,487
<i>But you can't buy justice.</i>

622
00:34:33,029 --> 00:34:37,909
<i>Now it's time for you to face</i>
<i>the consequences of your crimes.</i>

623
00:34:38,576 --> 00:34:40,953
[tense music playing]

624
00:34:52,632 --> 00:34:54,425
Ma'am! Who filed the case against you?

625
00:34:54,509 --> 00:34:56,010
Is there any truth to their accusations?

626
00:34:56,427 --> 00:34:57,887
Ma'am, please answer the question!

627
00:34:57,970 --> 00:35:00,056
-Out of the way.
-Ma'am, what did you do?

628
00:35:00,139 --> 00:35:01,307
Why were you arrested?

629
00:35:01,390 --> 00:35:03,893
[reporters clamoring]

630
00:35:03,976 --> 00:35:05,978
Ma'am, is there any truth
to their accusations?

631
00:35:06,062 --> 00:35:09,107
[reporters clamoring]

632
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:13,945
I have no intentions of going
to that dingy, stinking jail.

633
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:15,154
What?!

634
00:35:15,238 --> 00:35:18,074
Earlier, you hid Emilia from the police.

635
00:35:19,408 --> 00:35:21,869
Julio, your daughter needs you.

636
00:35:27,458 --> 00:35:30,002
I don't have a daughter who's a criminal.

637
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:32,922
And, most importantly,
I don't have a daughter

638
00:35:33,005 --> 00:35:36,634
who's dumb enough
to get caught for her crimes!

639
00:35:39,428 --> 00:35:40,680
Okay, I must admit…

640
00:35:41,681 --> 00:35:43,724
I tried to hide her

641
00:35:43,808 --> 00:35:45,643
when I thought there was
the slimmest chance

642
00:35:45,726 --> 00:35:47,019
that she might be able to escape.

643
00:35:48,062 --> 00:35:51,357
But now that everybody's
feasting on her downfall,

644
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:56,487
I won't dirty my hands
with the mess she made!

645
00:35:56,571 --> 00:36:00,032
Well then, whether you like it
or not, I'm going to her.

646
00:36:00,449 --> 00:36:02,577
Go ahead! I'm not going to stop you!

647
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:05,454
Anyway, what else can you do?

648
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:10,960
What else can you offer her
besides your cheap sympathy?

649
00:36:13,087 --> 00:36:14,547
I won't stoop to your level.

650
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:17,800
You're worse than the devil himself.

651
00:36:19,844 --> 00:36:21,137
That hurts!

652
00:36:23,764 --> 00:36:24,682
Well…

653
00:36:25,391 --> 00:36:26,726
What a softie.

654
00:36:27,435 --> 00:36:28,394
But anyway…

655
00:36:28,561 --> 00:36:29,937
You know, I realized…

656
00:36:30,980 --> 00:36:33,357
she's not an Ardiente.

657
00:36:35,318 --> 00:36:37,028
But seriously, Congressman,

658
00:36:37,111 --> 00:36:39,530
what do you plan to do with Emilia?

659
00:36:40,031 --> 00:36:41,282
Emilia…

660
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:46,120
will have a staycation in jail
for as long as necessary.

661
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:50,041
Now, when I think and know
that the time is right,

662
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:54,337
I will bail her out myself.

663
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:55,796
Well…

664
00:36:56,464 --> 00:36:59,425
It will all depend on how things turn out.

665
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:03,763
[chuckles]

666
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:07,141
Poor Emilia.

667
00:37:08,309 --> 00:37:11,437
[somber music playing]

668
00:37:15,399 --> 00:37:16,984
Emilia has been arrested!

669
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:21,322
Thank you so much, Diego!
Thanks to you and Ivy!

670
00:37:21,697 --> 00:37:23,699
We should be the ones thanking you.

671
00:37:24,158 --> 00:37:26,619
Thank you for the trust
you gave me and Ivy.

672
00:37:26,994 --> 00:37:28,371
But it doesn't end here.

673
00:37:29,247 --> 00:37:31,999
We need to put Emilia Ardiente in prison.

674
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:35,670
Attorney Fisher called too.

675
00:37:36,254 --> 00:37:39,382
She'll schedule trials
as soon as possible.

676
00:37:39,465 --> 00:37:41,717
Then, until the trials start,

677
00:37:41,968 --> 00:37:44,011
we'll be keeping you from Emilia.

678
00:37:44,512 --> 00:37:45,638
Don't worry.

679
00:37:46,305 --> 00:37:48,140
We're here to protect you.

680
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:49,642
Thank you.

681
00:37:51,978 --> 00:37:54,438
[dramatic music playing]

682
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:10,538
[suspenseful music playing]

683
00:38:15,001 --> 00:38:19,880
[Ivy] <i>As much as I'd like</i>
<i>to pity you, Emilia, I won't.</i>

684
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:23,259
<i>Because you deserve to be in prison.</i>

685
00:38:24,385 --> 00:38:26,637
<i>And I won't even celebrate this</i>

686
00:38:26,721 --> 00:38:31,350
<i>because seeking justice isn't a game.</i>

687
00:38:32,143 --> 00:38:33,936
<i>It's a responsibility.</i>

688
00:38:36,480 --> 00:38:38,190
[tense music playing]

689
00:38:39,734 --> 00:38:40,901
Come in, Madam.

690
00:38:40,985 --> 00:38:42,778
For now, you'll be staying
in the Chief's office.

691
00:38:52,913 --> 00:38:54,457
Do you know who this is?

692
00:39:02,173 --> 00:39:04,884
Excuse me, Madam. Please fill this up.

693
00:39:05,134 --> 00:39:07,011
You haven't even answered my question!

694
00:39:07,428 --> 00:39:08,721
How rude!

695
00:39:09,513 --> 00:39:11,891
I was asking if you knew who this was.

696
00:39:12,558 --> 00:39:14,602
Yes. You're Mrs. Emilia,

697
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:17,980
former Mayor and Governor
of Poblacion Ardiente.

698
00:39:18,731 --> 00:39:21,317
But right now,
we're just following our SOP.

699
00:39:21,400 --> 00:39:22,735
And, you have to comply with them.

700
00:39:23,319 --> 00:39:24,070
Excuse me.

701
00:39:24,153 --> 00:39:26,405
I don't have to learn your stupid SOP

702
00:39:26,489 --> 00:39:29,742
because I'm getting out of here!
I'm not staying here!

703
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:34,205
So, don't you ever teach me to
follow your stupid SOP, okay?!

704
00:39:35,247 --> 00:39:36,082
Now…

705
00:39:36,957 --> 00:39:39,960
If you don't treat me with respect,

706
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:41,712
I'll have to book you for a "good job".

707
00:39:42,922 --> 00:39:44,507
Do you know what that means?

708
00:39:44,965 --> 00:39:48,010
I can order someone to kill you
and your family!

709
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:51,639
Then, when the deed is done,
I'll say "good job".

710
00:39:52,139 --> 00:39:55,851
Now, are you going to
treat me with respect,

711
00:39:56,102 --> 00:39:58,187
or are you going to get the "good job"?

712
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:02,858
[slow tense music playing]

713
00:40:15,955 --> 00:40:16,872
Lily…

714
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:20,876
I hope that Julio doesn't
have that daughter of his freed.

715
00:40:21,252 --> 00:40:23,963
I've had it with that Emilia.

716
00:40:24,505 --> 00:40:27,091
I might just give her a piece of my mind.

717
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:28,467
Mom…

718
00:40:29,427 --> 00:40:32,054
You were just discharged
from the hospital.

719
00:40:33,556 --> 00:40:35,057
Don't worry about it.

720
00:40:35,141 --> 00:40:38,853
I assure you Julio
won't have Emilia freed.

721
00:40:38,936 --> 00:40:42,231
And even if he does, I'll stop him.

722
00:40:42,314 --> 00:40:44,775
I'll find a way to protect you from her.

723
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:48,696
And I will, Mom. I promise you that.

724
00:40:49,447 --> 00:40:50,948
[pensive music playing]

725
00:40:52,324 --> 00:40:55,244
I'm sorry, Lily.

726
00:40:56,328 --> 00:41:00,207
I just can't help but worry
that she'll escape from prison.

727
00:41:00,916 --> 00:41:04,712
Like, what if her men are just out there,

728
00:41:04,795 --> 00:41:08,048
waiting for the right time to strike?

729
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:09,133
To hurt us?

730
00:41:09,967 --> 00:41:11,469
To hurt you?

731
00:41:12,219 --> 00:41:13,095
Mom…

732
00:41:14,054 --> 00:41:18,184
Emilia Ardiente can't lay a hand on me.

733
00:41:18,267 --> 00:41:21,770
And, definitely not you.

734
00:41:22,688 --> 00:41:24,106
And, in case she does,

735
00:41:24,356 --> 00:41:27,860
I'll do everything in my power

736
00:41:27,943 --> 00:41:29,236
to make her own father

737
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:33,199
betray her, to make her
lose her title as an Ardiente.

738
00:41:35,534 --> 00:41:38,162
There's no way Emilia can run from me now.

739
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:44,043
This is revenge for everything
she's done to our family.

740
00:41:44,126 --> 00:41:48,172
I'm going to make sure
that Emilia rots behind bars,

741
00:41:48,255 --> 00:41:51,967
both her body and her soul.

742
00:42:09,568 --> 00:42:12,696
-Emilia…
-Auntie! Auntie!

743
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:13,948
Are you okay?

744
00:42:14,573 --> 00:42:16,283
Auntie, I'm glad you came.

745
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:18,452
Where's Papa and my lawyer?

746
00:42:19,286 --> 00:42:21,914
[suspenseful music playing]

747
00:42:21,997 --> 00:42:24,500
Auntie, don't tell me you're not
going to bail me out of here?

748
00:42:25,125 --> 00:42:27,127
So, why did you even come here?

749
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:29,588
I'm just here to comfort you.

750
00:42:29,672 --> 00:42:32,299
Auntie, it's not like I'm going to die.

751
00:42:32,800 --> 00:42:35,594
What I need is I want to get out of here!

752
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:36,804
I don't belong here!

753
00:42:37,596 --> 00:42:38,347
Auntie…

754
00:42:38,430 --> 00:42:39,682
I'm sorry.

755
00:42:41,058 --> 00:42:42,726
I don't like it here!

756
00:42:42,810 --> 00:42:46,188
Madam, the Chief said
he needs you to leave this room.

757
00:42:46,897 --> 00:42:48,274
We'll be taking you to your cell.

758
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:49,108
-Wait, hold on.
-Let's go.

759
00:42:49,191 --> 00:42:50,776
You can't lock me up!

760
00:42:50,859 --> 00:42:52,111
-Sorry, Madam.
-Wait! Auntie!

761
00:42:52,194 --> 00:42:53,362
Don't touch me!

762
00:42:53,445 --> 00:42:54,863
-Please just cooperate.
-Emilia.

763
00:42:54,947 --> 00:42:56,198
-Please come with us.
-Auntie!

764
00:42:56,282 --> 00:42:58,117
-Please wait.
-Don't lock me up! You can't!

765
00:42:59,577 --> 00:43:01,954
[dramatic music playing]

766
00:43:31,358 --> 00:43:35,362
[somber music playing]

767
00:44:16,820 --> 00:44:19,114
[screaming]

768
00:44:22,743 --> 00:44:24,453
There's a cockroach!

769
00:44:24,536 --> 00:44:26,080
[squealing]

770
00:44:27,039 --> 00:44:28,332
Get me out of here!

771
00:44:28,415 --> 00:44:31,043
I can't do this. I don't belong here!

772
00:44:33,087 --> 00:44:34,129
Cockroach!

773
00:44:36,924 --> 00:44:41,011
[dramatic music playing]

774
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:49,186
<i>Why are you punishing your own daughter?</i>

775
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:50,104
<i>Just shut up!</i>

776
00:44:50,187 --> 00:44:51,021
<i>You'll eventually meet your maker.</i>

777
00:44:51,105 --> 00:44:53,065
<i>50 million pesos.</i>

778
00:44:53,148 --> 00:44:56,402
<i>If I help you, what will I get in return?</i>

779
00:44:56,485 --> 00:44:59,780
<i>I will become king and you will be queen.</i>

780
00:44:59,863 --> 00:45:01,573
<i>There's something you need to know.</i>

781
00:45:01,657 --> 00:45:04,034
<i>Who are you talking to?</i>

782
00:45:04,118 --> 00:45:05,327
<i>Please help me.</i>

783
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:07,162
<i>I'll help you, but on one condition.</i>

784
00:45:07,246 --> 00:45:08,705
<i>Turn your back on your father.</i>

785
00:45:11,291 --> 00:45:12,167
[gunshot]

786
00:45:14,128 --> 00:45:15,587
-[gunshot]
-[squeals]

787
00:45:18,590 --> 00:45:19,591
<i>Dante.</i>

788
00:45:19,675 --> 00:45:20,592
<i>Dad?</i>

789
00:45:20,676 --> 00:45:23,470
[theme music playing]
